{"seq":2,"at":"2026-10-20","kind":"edited","target":{"type":"article","id":"a1976"},"reason":"Rewritten by the merge to take in the printed cards' questions.","by":"merge belief/religion","ref":"quiz-archive/runs/tp-ingest/decisions/belief__religion.json","changes":[{"field":"bodyEn","diff":[["=",780],["+","Honoratus of Amiens, a bishop of Amiens in northern France who died around 600, is the patron saint of bakers, confectioners and sweet makers. The French remember Saint Honoré every year on 16 May, and Parisian pastry cooks named the gâteau Saint-Honoré, a crown of choux puffs filled with cream, after him, just as the rue du Faubourg Saint-Honoré takes its name from a church dedicated to him.\n\n"],["=",125],["+","\n| Honoratus of Amiens | bakers, confectioners | Saint-Honoré cake, rue Saint-Honoré |"]]},{"field":"bodyDe","diff":[["=",728],["+","Honoratus von Amiens, ein um 600 gestorbener Bischof von Amiens in Nordfrankreich, ist der Schutzpatron der Bäcker, Konditoren und Süßwarenhersteller. Die Franzosen gedenken des heiligen Honoré jedes Jahr am 16. Mai, und Pariser Konditoren benannten die Saint-Honoré-Torte, einen Kranz aus sahnegefüllten Windbeuteln, nach ihm, so wie die Rue du Faubourg Saint-Honoré ihren Namen einer ihm geweihten Kirche verdankt.\n\n"],["=",107],["+","\n| Honoratus von Amiens | Bäckern, Konditoren | Saint-Honoré-Torte, Rue Saint-Honoré |"]]}]},
